# .gitleaksignore — accepted-risk suppression list for gitleaks
#
# Format: one SHA256 fingerprint per line (the `Fingerprint` field from
# gitleaks JSON output). Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# How to add an entry:
#   1. Run: npm run scan:secrets  (or: gitleaks detect --source . --report-format json)
#   2. Confirm the flagged value is a dummy / non-sensitive credential
#   3. Copy the `Fingerprint` field from the JSON report and paste it below
#   4. Add a comment on the next line explaining why it is safe to suppress
#
# No entries currently needed — gitleaks finds no leaks in the codebase.
# If a future rule change causes test fixtures containing dummy credential-shaped
# strings to be flagged (e.g. values like `sk-brave-test` in
# src/search/fanout.paid.test.ts), add the fingerprints here rather than
# deleting or obfuscating the test data.
